---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="How this site is built">
  <div class="page">
    <h1>How this site is built</h1>
    <p>This site is a static site built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>.</p>
    <p>
      Originally <a href="https://www.harrytrimble.com/">Harry</a> built the site with Bootstrap and some gnarly jQuery
      soup, which made it slow and expensive. Thankfully, <a href="http://tommyp.org/">Tommy</a> got involved and changed
      all that, with Next.js and Tailwind. In 2026 it was rebuilt again so it could keep up with councils being created,
      merged and abolished.
    </p>

    <h3>Councils</h3>
    <p>
      Every council the site knows about, past, present and scheduled, is in one data file. It started from the
      government's open registers of local authorities in England, Northern Ireland, Scotland and Wales, which were
      switched off in 2021. Each council is matched to its <a href="https://www.ons.gov.uk/methodology/geography/ukgeographies/administrativegeography">ONS code</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reorganisations are dates in that file, so the site works out what's current each time it's built. When a council is
      abolished its bin moves to Retro, and its page points to whoever took over.
    </p>

    <h3>The map</h3>
    <p>
      The <a href="/map">map</a> is drawn when the site is built, from{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/ONSvisual/topojson_boundaries">ONS boundaries</a> for 2022. Councils created since then
      are drawn by joining together the councils they replaced.
    </p>

    <h3>Hosting and privacy</h3>
    <p>
      Hosted on <a href="https://www.netlify.com/">Netlify</a>, the site{" "}
      <a href="https://plausible.io/govbins.uk">counts page views and visitors</a> using aggregated data, anonymised.
      Meaning the site doesn't use cookies or any other potentially creepy tracking stuff.
    </p>

    <h3>Web performance</h3>
    <p>
      Photos are resized and converted to WebP when the site is built, and load as you scroll. The homepage works without
      JavaScript; sorting is the only thing that needs it.
    </p>

    <h3>Open code</h3>
    <p>Go to <a href="https://github.com/govbins/govbins.uk">GitHub</a> to look at all the code for this site.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
